  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "FND-34e1d3f1f4de46d4b2e9c551",
      "category": "UI_ASSERTION_GAP",
      "target_type": "CRITERION",
      "target_id": "CRT-f1e97d3e088b6b145a26afec",
      "blocking": true,
      "finding": "Neither geometry assertion is discriminating as planned. The browser observation is run with device metrics whose width is taken from the assertion's own viewport (402) and whose height is taken from the expected height rule value (874), so the emulated viewport equals the expected frame box. A viewport-relative implementation (width:100%, height:100vh) measures exactly 402x874 and satisfies both EQUALS rules at tolerance 0 without ever realizing the fixed 402pt/874pt reference. The FUNCTIONAL_TEST side cannot compensate, because its expected text only requires the width/height CSS declarations to be 'present'. The retained screenshot is likewise non-discriminating: it is captured with captureBeyondViewport:false at the same metrics. Height in particular has no oracle anywhere in the plan that is independent of the viewport chosen to measure it.",
      "evidence": [
        "AST-4c180398b652ac55717834c0 / AST-f467d4d399982892fd953eae expected — {\"kind\":\"EQUALS\",\"tolerance\":0,\"unit\":\"pt\",\"value\":402} and value 874",
        "PROOF-5bf70c142664f62885a0b52f expected — 'width/height CSS declarations and title text are present'",
        "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:40 — `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride({width:viewport,height,deviceScaleFactor:1,mobile:false})`",
        "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:55 — `Page.captureScreenshot({format:'png',captureBeyondViewport:false})`",
        "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:71 — `viewport:frame.rule.viewports[0],height:required.find(d=>d.property==='height').rule.value` (device metrics = the expected values)"
      ],
      "required_correction": "Make the geometry criterion discriminating: require the Node obligation to assert the exact declared values (frame width:402px and height:874px in the rendered markup), and/or require the VISUAL_COMPARE observation to be taken with a device height different from the expected 874 so that a viewport-relative frame cannot satisfy the height assertion.",
      "dependency_target_ids": [
        "AST-4c180398b652ac55717834c0",
        "AST-f467d4d399982892fd953eae",
        "IMP-2f098fe113297ed481965d7d",
        "PLAN-e79fd9baf64e417ed65480fd",
        "PROOF-5bf70c142664f62885a0b52f",
        "PROOF-7d83cc32dc5249b4ce221b29",
        "REQ-281504b7efe6228214f137ca"
      ],
      "reentry_stage": "PLAN"
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "FND-9dabb5bde90fba5e45a7acb9",
      "category": "TEST_GAP",
      "target_type": "TEST",
      "target_id": "TEST-e5f983bddef9f05c7b7df113",
      "blocking": true,
      "finding": "The expected text of this test obligation requires only presence, not equality: 'the frame and title data-figma-id locators, width/height CSS declarations and title text are present'. A render() emitting data-figma-id=\"4478:7209\" with width:1px;height:1px satisfies it literally. No Node-executed obligation in the plan therefore pins the frozen 402/874 values, which leaves the geometry entirely dependent on the VISUAL_COMPARE route weakened by the two preceding findings. (The 'Zones corporelles' content assertion is not affected in the same way: textContent is compared exactly by the observer with no subject-controlled adjustment, so the identical wording in TEST-d437f04e0b6969ae349c2b0e is backed elsewhere.)",
      "evidence": [
        "TEST-e5f983bddef9f05c7b7df113 expected — 'Execute Screen.render() and inspect its HTML markup: the frame and title data-figma-id locators, width/height CSS declarations and title text are present.'",
        "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-recipe.js:25-26 — `const expected=qualificationContract?[(visual?qualificationContract.visual_test_expected:r.statement),qualificationContract.preservation_test_expected].join(' '):r.statement;` reused verbatim for test_obligations and the FUNCTIONAL_TEST proof",
        "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:17 — the shared `visual_test_expected` string from which this obligation and PROOF-5bf70c142664f62885a0b52f are generated",
        "tests/ui.test.js@301d6dd — current content `const s=require('../src/features/example/Screen');if(!s)throw Error('fixture');` has no value assertion to build on"
      ],
      "required_correction": "Restate the expected text of this obligation (and of PROOF-5bf70c142664f62885a0b52f) to require exact equality against the frozen reference — the frame declares width:402px and height:874px — instead of mere presence, keeping the existing disclaimer that rendered geometry is additionally measured by the separate browser observer.",
      "dependency_target_ids": [
        "CAND-d014bbb30ee04961b625b2e3",
        "IMP-393537ac37c70c77bd5c40ea",
        "PLAN-e79fd9baf64e417ed65480fd",
        "PROOF-5bf70c142664f62885a0b52f",
        "REQ-281504b7efe6228214f137ca"
      ],
      "reentry_stage": "PLAN"
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "FND-ba2cf58168018af5d845dc01",
      "category": "PROOF_GAP",
      "target_type": "PROOF",
      "target_id": "PROOF-7d83cc32dc5249b4ce221b29",
      "blocking": true,
      "finding": "The VISUAL_COMPARE obligation is the only obligation in the plan that can pin the frame width to the frozen 402, but the observer that executes it is not independent of the subject under test. Before measuring, it reads a numeric constant exported by the delivered Screen.js (`subject.__figmaWidthDelta`) and mutates the frame with it, then re-reads getBoundingClientRect. An implementation that renders a non-conforming width (e.g. 400px) and exports a compensating delta of 2 is reported as width 402 and passes. This directly contradicts the justification carried into every change intent of this plan item, which states the trusted browser 'checks the reference without reading numeric return constants'. The driver uses the same hook deliberately in the inflating direction to demonstrate rejection (qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:108), which confirms the hook is live; nothing in the plan forbids the subject from using it in the compensating direction, and src/features/example/Screen.js is inside write_scope.",
      "evidence": [
        "planContract PLAN-e79fd9baf64e417ed65480fd / impact IMP-2f098fe113297ed481965d7d impact_reason — 'A trusted separate browser measures getBoundingClientRect and textContent at viewport 402, retains a screenshot, and checks the reference without reading numeric return constants.'",
        "planContract.boundaries.write_scope includes src/features/example/Screen.js (CAND-e35fa3f158e08d087bf37096), so the subject can author the delta export",
        "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:48 — `if(subject.__figmaWidthDelta)frame.style.width=(frame.getBoundingClientRect().width+subject.__figmaWidthDelta)+'px';`",
        "scripts/kodjo/lib/vnext-figma-browser-observer.js:49,51 — `const rect=frame.getBoundingClientRect()` ... `return {viewport:innerWidth,width:rect.width,...}` (the adjusted rect is what is reported)",
        "scripts/kodjo/qualify-vnext-figma-real-path.js:108 — `fs.appendFileSync(path.join(f.cwd,SCREEN),'\\nmodule.exports.__figmaWidthDelta = 1;\\n')` shows the subject export reaches the observer"
      ],
      "required_correction": "Correct the VISUAL_COMPARE obligation and the shared observer intent so they state what the executor actually does, and close the channel: require that the measured geometry be read with no subject-exported adjustment applied (observer ignores `__figmaWidthDelta` outside the driver's own negative control), and add an implementation_constraint to PLAN-e79fd9baf64e417ed65480fd forbidding any export of src/features/example/Screen.js that influences the observer's measurement.",
      "dependency_target_ids": [
        "AST-4c180398b652ac55717834c0",
        "CAND-e35fa3f158e08d087bf37096",
        "IMP-2f098fe113297ed481965d7d",
        "PLAN-e79fd9baf64e417ed65480fd",
        "REQ-281504b7efe6228214f137ca"
      ],
      "reentry_stage": "PLAN"
    }
  ],
